<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10080" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιλαγχάνω</span></b> , pf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-είληχα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					40.3
				</span></i>
			:—as law-term, <i>move for a rehearing of a
			suit,</i> when the case had gone by default, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. δίαιταν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					21.86
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὴν μὴ οὖσαν</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίαιταν</span>) ib.<i><span class="en">
				90
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				8.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἔρημον</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκην</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					32.27
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>enter an exceptive plea,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ νόμοι διδόασι τὰς παραγραφὰς
					ἀντιλαγχάνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					37.33
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>bring counteraction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Arc.</u>
				17
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
